towers (working title): credits and licences

Code: this repository (MIT, see LICENSE). Every model, texture, colour grade, effect sheet, map and sound is generated
by code in this repository or its sibling example repositories; no third-party art or audio is shipped, so there is
nothing further to attribute.

Where each asset comes from
- assets/models/tower_*, pad, core, portal, shell, lamp, decor_*: modelled by tools/blender/towerkit.py (with
  crawler_lib.py and cwchar_lib.py from crawler), run headless in Blender (Blender is used as a tool; its output is
  ours). towers.json (the muzzle points) is written by the same script.
- assets/models/skitter, ghoul, hound, imp, sporeling, bloater, shade, ogre: crawler's creatures (more-cartwheel-examples,
  games/crawler), as they are.
- assets/maps/*.cwtd: tools/gen-maps.mjs. assets/lightmaps/*.cwlm and *.hash: baked by towers_mapview (tools/mapview).
- assets/textures/*.png: tools/gen-textures.mjs. assets/grade/*.cube: tools/gen-luts.mjs.
- assets/fx/fire.png, fire_mv.png, smoke.png, smoke_mv.png, scorch.png, haze.png: crawler's copies (scorch.png lightened
  so its darkest multiplies the ground by about 0.56, never a black hole on a pale path; baked by
  cartwheel-engine's tools/fx/bake-flipbooks.mjs and hordeshooter's gen-fx-sheets.mjs; procedural, CC0).
- The creeps' crowd, the flow field and the effect kit follow crawler's and hordeshooter's code (sim.c, view.c, fx.c).
- Sounds: synthesised in main.c.
